title: '[pallet-bounties] allow closing/awarding bounties with active child bounties'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    resolves https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/10790

    Previously the parent bounty `award_bounty` and `close_bounty` calls were blocked whenever the
    bounty had active child bounties. This let a curator prevent governance from closing a bounty
    simply by keeping a child bounty active.

    These calls now proactively close all active child bounties of the parent bounty via the new
    `ChildBountyManager::close_child_bounties` method: every child bounty curator deposit is
    refunded, the child bounty funds are returned to the parent bounty account and the child bounty
    storage is cleared, so no orphaned child bounty (a child without a parent) is left behind. The
    parent calls reserve the worst-case weight (`MaxActiveChildBountyCount` child bounties) up front
    and refund the unused weight via `PostDispatchInfo`; `award_bounty` now returns
    `DispatchResultWithPostInfo`.

    The `ChildBountyManager` trait gains `close_child_bounties` (now returning the consumed weight)
    and `close_child_bounties_max_weight`; runtimes implementing this trait manually must update
    their implementation.
crates:
- name: pallet-bounties
  bump: major
- name: pallet-child-bounties
  bump: minor
